From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 02:27:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 126/128] dynarmic A64: float loads straight into XMM registers
 (LDR S/D with fastmem)

A 32- or 64-bit plain load whose one use widens it to a quad (LDR S/D into a vector register)
is a movd/movq xmm, [mem] (the other lanes zeroed), its widening nothing, instead of a load into
a general register and a movd/movq across. Fastmem sites only (A64EmitX64::PeepholeQuad marks
them); their fallbacks are stubs that put the callback's value into the XMM; a range-check miss
takes the fallback, a declined site the general-register path. game.c for AArch64: -1.9%.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01REmpC53sSK3VTcKMxWFSSb
